# Every file in this tree is checked out with LF line endings.
#
# §219: the tree's gates read the tree's text and compare it with other text
# in the tree -- an anchor with the file it names, a block of prose with the
# code it quotes. A checkout that rewrites the line endings makes the same
# tree read differently on different machines, and the comparison stops
# answering the same question.
#
# The first thing that broke was the anchors gate on Windows: the script it
# reads was CRLF there and LF here, and the gate could not find a single
# anchor in it. The tree says how it is checked out; this file is that say.
#
# `text=auto` leaves the binary files to git -- it detects them -- and
# `eol=lf` gives every text file the same ending on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf
